From 5d52689d2201ea9d3cdaf3f80ae40ba0b21edda1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "claude[bot]" <41898282+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 08:56:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Support whole-column, whole-row, and open-ended ranges

The REF/REFRANGE lexer tokens required both a column and a row on
every endpoint, so Excel / Google Sheets shapes like A:A (whole
column), 1:1 (whole row), and A1:B (open-ended) failed to lex and
evaluated to #ERROR!.

Factor REF into COL/ROW fragments and extend REFRANGE to accept the
partial-endpoint forms. Because ranges are modeled as concrete
[from, to] cell pairs, unbounded ranges are clamped to the sheet's
data extent up front: Store.getUsedBounds() (via CellIndex.bounds())
feeds expandUnboundedRanges(), which rewrites each local unbounded
reference to a concrete range before extraction, grid fetch, and
evaluation. The calculator and buildDependantsMap apply the same
rewrite so column/row edits still trigger recalculation.

Range aggregations now skip blank cells (Arguments.iterate),
matching Google Sheets, so AVERAGE/MIN/MAX/COUNT over a whole column
ignore empty cells instead of counting them as 0.

Fixes #280

