Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Skip tokenization for colon-free formulas in range
 expansion

expandUnboundedRanges runs for every formula cell in buildDependantsMap
(on each edit). An unbounded range always contains ':', so a colon-free
formula can bail out before tokenizing, keeping the common case free.
Add a mixed-formula test confirming token concatenation round-trips
strings and operators around the rewritten refs.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (autonomous)
---
 packages/sheets/src/formula/formula.ts       |  4 +++-
 packages/sheets/test/formula/formula.test.ts | 12 ++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/packages/sheets/src/formula/formula.ts b/packages/sheets/src/formula/formula.ts
index 18537646f..b36594bfd 100644
--- a/packages/sheets/src/formula/formula.ts
+++ b/packages/sheets/src/formula/formula.ts
@@ -352,7 +352,9 @@ export function expandUnboundedRanges(
   formula: string,
   bounds: Range | undefined,
 ): string {
-  if (!formula.startsWith('=')) {
+  // Fast path: an unbounded range always contains ':', so a colon-free formula
+  // (the common case) never needs rewriting and skips tokenization entirely.
+  if (!formula.startsWith('=') || !formula.includes(':')) {
     return formula;
   }
 
